<title>FRANCE: TENNIS-CAPRIATI PULLS OUT OF FRENCH OPEN.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-CAPRIATI PULLS OUT OF FRENCH OPEN.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Jennifer Capriati pulled out of the French tennis Open with an ankle injury, organisers said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The 21-year-old Capriati, now out of the top 20, made history at the French Open in 1990 when she became the youngest-ever semifinalist in a grand slam tournament.</p>
<p>She will be replaced in the women's draw by Russian Tatyana Panova.</p>
